European human rights law, particularly as articulated through the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR) and the jurisprudence of the European Court of Human Rights (ECtHR), emphasizes the principles of equality and non-discrimination as fundamental rights. These principles are enshrined primarily in Article 14 of the ECHR, which prohibits discrimination on various grounds, including race, sex, religion, and political opinion, among others. 

